Breakpoint does not redistribute upstream source code or model weights. The ACT deployment stress
benchmark uses the following projects at run time. Each is obtained by its own
installer or download and stays under its own license.

- LeRobot (https://github.com/huggingface/lerobot), Apache-2.0. Pinned to commit
  3c0a209f9fac4d2a57617e686a7f2a2309144ba2 and cloned into vendor/ by the setup
  commands; vendor/ is not tracked in this repository.
- lerobot/act_aloha_sim_transfer_cube_human weights (Hugging Face Hub), license
  apache-2.0 as stated on the model card. The ACT method is described in
  "Learning Fine-Grained Bimanual Manipulation with Low-Cost Hardware"
  (https://arxiv.org/abs/2304.13705).
- gym-aloha (https://github.com/huggingface/gym-aloha), Apache-2.0, which provides
  the simulated ALOHA transfer-cube task.
- MuJoCo and dm_control (Google DeepMind), Apache-2.0, installed as dependencies of
  gym-aloha.
- ONNX, ONNX Runtime, NumPy, Matplotlib, PyAV, OpenCV, PyTorch and torchvision are
  installed from PyPI under their own licenses. Check each package's metadata
  before redistributing an environment.

The comparison media under benchmarks/act-transfer/deployment-stress/media/ are frames rendered
from that simulator with the model above. Exported ONNX graphs are not tracked; their
SHA-256 values are recorded in
benchmarks/act-transfer/deployment-stress/data/protocol/v1_protocol_lock.json.

Names of third-party projects are used only to identify them. This project is not
affiliated with or endorsed by their owners.
